      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "summary",
          "text": "Release of OpenShift Serverless Logic 1.35.0\n\nRed Hat Product Security has rated this update as having a security impact of Important. A Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE link(s) in the References section.",
          "title": "Topic"
        },
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "This release includes security, bug fixes, and enhancements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* com.graphql-java/graphql-java: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in GraphQL Java (CVE-2024-40094)\n\n* openshift-serverless-1-logic-rhel8-operator-container: encoding/protojson, internal/encoding/json: infinite loop in protojson.Unmarshal when unmarshaling certain forms of invalid JSON (CVE-2024-24786)\n\n* path-to-regexp: Backtracking regular expressions cause ReDoS (CVE-2024-45296)\n\nFor more details about the security issues, including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgements, and other related information, refer to the CVE pages listed in the References section.",
          "title": "Details"
        },
        {
